/*
mounts
------

Adds extra mounts to the container.
Each entry follows the syntax of Docker’s `--mount` flag and can reference
environment or predefined variables.

Default: *unset*.

Example:
  "mounts": [
    { "type": "volume",
      "source": "dind-var-lib-docker",
      "target": "/var/lib/docker" }
  ]

Choosing a mount type
• **Bind mount** – Ideal when you need to edit files on the host and have
  changes appear instantly in the container.
• **Volume** – Better for data that should persist across container runs but
  doesn’t need to live on the host filesystem.
*/

{
  "name": "1_15-spec_mounts",
  "image": "ubuntu:latest",

  "mounts": [{
    "source": "${localEnv:HOME}",
    "target": "/hostHome",
    "type": "bind"
  }, {
    "source": "mount",
    "target": "/volume/mount",
    "type": "volume"
  }]
}
